        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, thank you for referring this 85-year-old gentleman, admitted on 21/09/1986 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination confirmed widespread expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia with compensated respiratory acidosis. Blood tests showed a mild inflammatory response. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and monitored closely with pulse oximetry and regular vital signs. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He is discharged home with a course of oral prednisolone and optimised inhaler therapy. Please arrange follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. I remain available for any queries.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
